{"id":"mahabharata-9-018","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":18,"title":"अष्टादशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 18 · The Kauravas fall into disarray","summary":{"en":"With Shalya slain the Kaurava sons and warriors lose heart, and Shakuni urges them to fight on to win the war. The Pandavas, rejoicing, attack to seize the Kaurava king and slaughter many of his followers.","kn":"ಶಲ್ಯ ಹತನಾದ ಮೇಲೆ ಕೌರವ ಮಕ್ಕಳು, ವೀರರು ಧೈರ್ಯ ಕಳೆದುಕೊಳ್ಳುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಯುದ್ಧ ಗೆಲ್ಲಲು ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಿರಲು ಶಕುನಿ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಹರ್ಷಗೊಂಡ ಪಾಂಡವರು ಕೌರವ ರಾಜನನ್ನು ಹಿಡಿಯಲು ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡಿ ಅನುಯಾಯಿಗಳನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"शल्य के मरने पर कौरव पुत्र और योद्धा हताश हो जाते हैं, और शकुनि उन्हें युद्ध जीतने तक लड़ने को कहता है। हर्षित पाण्डव कौरव राजा को पकड़ने के लिए आक्रमण करते हैं और उसके बहुत अनुयायियों को मारते हैं।","te":"శల్యుడు చనిపోయాక కౌరవ కుమారులు, వీరులు ధైర్యం కోల్పోతారు; యుద్ధం గెలవడానికి పోరాడమని శకుని చెబుతాడు. ఆనందించిన పాండవులు కౌరవ రాజును పట్టుకోవడానికి దాడి చేసి అతని అనుచరులను చంపుతారు.","ta":"சல்யன் மாண்டதும் கௌரவ மக்களும் வீரரும் மனம் தளர, போரை வெல்லப் போரிடும்படி சகுனி கூறுகிறான். மகிழ்ந்த பாண்டவர் கௌரவ மன்னனைப் பிடிக்கத் தாக்கி அவன் ஆட்களைக் கொல்கின்றனர்.","ml":"ശല്യൻ വീണതോടെ കൗരവപുത്രന്മാരും യോദ്ധാക്കളും ധൈര്യം നഷ്ടപ്പെടുന്നു; യുദ്ധം ജയിക്കാൻ പൊരുതിത്തുടരണമെന്ന് ശകുനി അവരോട് പറയുന്നു. സന്തോഷിക്കുന്ന പാണ്ഡവർ കൗരവരാജാവിനെ പിടിക്കാൻ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു, അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ അനുയായികളിൽ പലരെയും കൊല്ലുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.18; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पातिते युधि दुर्धर्षे मद्रराजे महारथे ।\nतावकास्तव पुत्राश्च प्रायशो विमुखाभवन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the unconquerable great chariot-fighter, the king of the Madras, was struck down in battle, your warriors and your sons for the most part turned away."}},{"n":2,"text":"वणिजो नावि भिन्नायां यथागाधेऽप्लवेऽर्णवे ।\nअपारे पारमिच्छन्तो हते शूरे महात्मनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"They were like merchants on a broken ship in a fathomless, boundless sea, longing for the far shore, now that the great-souled hero was dead."}},{"n":3,"text":"मद्रराजे महाराज वित्रस्ताः शरविक्षताः ।\nअनाथा नाथमिच्छन्तो मृगाः सिंहार्दिता इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"With the Madra king gone, O great king, they were terrified and wounded by arrows, helpless and seeking a protector, like deer tormented by a lion."}},{"n":4,"text":"वृषा यथा भग्नशृङ्गाः शीर्णदन्ता गजा इव ।\nमध्याह्ने प्रत्यपायाम निर्जिता धर्मसूनुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like bulls with broken horns or elephants with shattered tusks, we withdrew at midday, defeated by the son of Dharma."}},{"n":5,"text":"न संधातुमनीकानि न च राजन्पराक्रमे ।\nआसीद्बुद्धिर्हते शल्ये तव योधस्य कस्यचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once Shalya was dead, O king, none of your warriors had the mind to re-form the ranks or to show valor."}},{"n":6,"text":"भीष्मे द्रोणे च निहते सूतपुत्रे च भारत ।\nयद्दुःखं तव योधानां भयं चासीद्विशां पते ।\nतद्भयं स च नः शोको भूय एवाभ्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The grief and fear your warriors felt when Bhishma, Drona and the charioteer's son Karna fell, O Bharata, lord of the people, came upon us again, together with sorrow."}},{"n":7,"text":"निराशाश्च जये तस्मिन्हते शल्ये महारथे ।\nहतप्रवीरा विध्वस्ता विकृत्ताश्च शितैः शरैः ।\nमद्रराजे हते राजन्योधास्ते प्राद्रवन्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hopeless of victory once the great chariot-fighter Shalya was dead, their heroes slain, broken and cut by sharp arrows, those warriors fled in fear, O king, when the Madra king fell."}},{"n":8,"text":"अश्वानन्ये गजानन्ये रथानन्ये महारथाः ।\nआरुह्य जवसंपन्नाः पादाताः प्राद्रवन्भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some great warriors mounted horses, some elephants, some chariots, and others ran away on foot in fear, all moving as fast as they could."}},{"n":9,"text":"द्विसाहस्राश्च मातङ्गा गिरिरूपाः प्रहारिणः ।\nसंप्राद्रवन्हते शल्ये अङ्कुशाङ्गुष्ठचोदिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Two thousand hard-hitting elephants, huge as hills, bolted when Shalya was killed, driven on by the goad and the toe."}},{"n":10,"text":"ते रणाद्भरतश्रेष्ठ तावकाः प्राद्रवन्दिशः ।\nधावन्तश्चाप्यदृश्यन्त श्वसमानाः शरातुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your men, best of the Bharatas, fled the battlefield in all directions; they were seen running, panting, tormented by arrows."}},{"n":11,"text":"तान्प्रभग्नान्द्रुतान्दृष्ट्वा हतोत्साहान्पराजितान् ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्त पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवाश्च जयैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them broken, fleeing, disheartened and defeated, the Panchalas and the Pandavas, eager for victory, pursued them."}},{"n":12,"text":"बाणशब्दरवश्चापि सिंहनादश्च पुष्कलः ।\nशङ्खशब्दश्च शूराणां दारुणः समपद्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fearful din rose up from the twang of bows, from abundant lion-roars and from the conches of the heroes."}},{"n":13,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु कौरवं सैन्यं भयत्रस्तं प्रविद्रुतम् ।\nअन्योन्यं समभाषन्त पाञ्चालाः पाण्डवैः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Kaurava army seized with fear and in flight, the Panchalas and Pandavas spoke to one another:"}},{"n":14,"text":"अद्य राजा सत्यधृतिर्जितामित्रो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nअद्य दुर्योधनो हीनो दीप्तया नृपतिश्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today King Yudhishthira, steadfast in truth, has defeated his enemies; today Duryodhana is stripped of his blazing royal glory.\""}},{"n":15,"text":"अद्य श्रुत्वा हतं पुत्रं धृतराष्ट्रो जनेश्वरः ।\nनिःसंज्ञः पतितो भूमौ किल्बिषं प्रतिपद्यताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today let King Dhritarashtra, hearing that his son is dead, fall senseless to the ground and bear the weight of his sin.\""}},{"n":16,"text":"अद्य जानातु कौन्तेयं समर्थं सर्वधन्विनाम् ।\nअद्यात्मानं च दुर्मेधा गर्हयिष्यति पापकृत् ।\nअद्य क्षत्तुर्वचः सत्यं स्मरतां ब्रुवतो हितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today let him know that the son of Kunti is the match of all archers. Today the sinful, foolish king will blame himself, and remember the true and beneficial words of Vidura as he spoke them.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"अद्यप्रभृति पार्थांश्च प्रेष्यभूत उपाचरन् ।\nविजानातु नृपो दुःखं यत्प्राप्तं पाण्डुनन्दनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"From today let him serve the sons of Pritha as a servant, and let the king understand the suffering the sons of Pandu have endured.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"अद्य कृष्णस्य माहात्म्यं जानातु स महीपतिः ।\nअद्यार्जुनधनुर्घोषं घोरं जानातु संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today let the king know the greatness of Krishna, and today let him know the fearful twang of Arjuna's bow in battle.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"अस्त्राणां च बलं सर्वं बाह्वोश्च बलमाहवे ।\nअद्य ज्ञास्यति भीमस्य बलं घोरं महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today he will learn the strength of the weapons and of the arms of the great-souled Bhima in the fight, and his terrible might.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"हते दुर्योधने युद्धे शक्रेणेवासुरे मये ।\nयत्कृतं भीमसेनेन दुःशासनवधे तदा ।\nनान्यः कर्तास्ति लोके तदृते भीमं महाबलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"When Duryodhana is slain in battle, as Indra slew the demon Maya, what Bhimasena did in killing Duhshasana, none but mighty Bhima in the world could do.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"जानीतामद्य ज्येष्ठस्य पाण्डवस्य पराक्रमम् ।\nमद्रराजं हतं श्रुत्वा देवैरपि सुदुःसहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let them know today the prowess of the eldest Pandava, which even the gods could not bear, now that they have heard the Madra king is dead.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"अद्य ज्ञास्यति संग्रामे माद्रीपुत्रौ महाबलौ ।\nनिहते सौबले शूरे गान्धारेषु च सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, with the heroic son of Subala dead and the Gandharas all slain, the two mighty sons of Madri will show themselves in battle.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"कथं तेषां जयो न स्याद्येषां योद्धा धनंजयः ।\nसात्यकिर्भीमसेनश्च धृष्टद्युम्नश्च पार्षतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How could those not win whose fighter is Arjuna, with Satyaki, Bhimasena and Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata?\""}},{"n":24,"text":"द्रौपद्यास्तनयाः पञ्च माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nशिखण्डी च महेष्वासो राजा चैव युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How could those not win who have the five sons of Draupadi, the two Pandava sons of Madri, the great archer Shikhandi and King Yudhishthira?\""}},{"n":25,"text":"येषां च जगतां नाथो नाथः कृष्णो जनार्दनः ।\nकथं तेषां जयो न स्याद्येषां धर्मो व्यपाश्रयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"How could those not win whose protector is Krishna, Janardana, lord of the worlds, and who take refuge in dharma?\""}},{"n":26,"text":"भीष्मं द्रोणं च कर्णं च मद्रराजानमेव च ।\nतथान्यान्नृपतीन्वीराञ्शतशोऽथ सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who else but Yudhishthira, son of Pritha, could conquer in battle Bhishma, Drona, Karna, the king of the Madras and other heroic kings by the hundreds and thousands?\""}},{"n":27,"text":"कोऽन्यः शक्तो रणे जेतुमृते पार्थं युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nयस्य नाथो हृषीकेशः सदा धर्मयशोनिधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Who else could do it, when his protector is Hrishikesha, ever a treasure of dharma and fame?\""}},{"n":28,"text":"इत्येवं वदमानास्ते हर्षेण महता युताः ।\nप्रभग्नांस्तावकान्राजन्सृञ्जयाः पृष्ठतोऽन्वयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So speaking, filled with great joy, the Srinjayas, O king, followed behind your fleeing men."}},{"n":29,"text":"धनंजयो रथानीकमभ्यवर्तत वीर्यवान् ।\nमाद्रीपुत्रौ च शकुनिं सात्यकिश्च महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Dhananjaya attacked the chariot division, and the two sons of Madri attacked Shakuni, with the great chariot-fighter Satyaki."}},{"n":30,"text":"तान्प्रेक्ष्य द्रवतः सर्वान्भीमसेनभयार्दितान् ।\nदुर्योधनस्तदा सूतमब्रवीदुत्स्मयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing all of them fleeing, tormented by fear of Bhimasena, Duryodhana then spoke to his charioteer, almost smiling."}},{"n":31,"text":"न मातिक्रमते पार्थो धनुष्पाणिमवस्थितम् ।\nजघने सर्वसैन्यानां ममाश्वान्प्रतिपादय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"The son of Pritha cannot pass me while I stand with bow in hand. Drive my horses to the rear of the whole army.\""}},{"n":32,"text":"जघने युध्यमानं हि कौन्तेयो मां धनंजयः ।\nनोत्सहेताभ्यतिक्रान्तुं वेलामिव महोदधिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If I am fighting at the rear, Arjuna, son of Kunti, will not be able to cross past me, as the great ocean cannot cross its shore.\""}},{"n":33,"text":"पश्य सैन्यं महत्सूत पाण्डवैः समभिद्रुतम् ।\nसैन्यरेणुं समुद्धूतं पश्यस्वैनं समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Look, charioteer, at the great army pursued by the Pandavas; look at the dust of the host raised on every side.\""}},{"n":34,"text":"सिंहनादांश्च बहुशः शृणु घोरान्भयानकान् ।\nतस्माद्याहि शनैः सूत जघनं परिपालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Listen to the lion-roars, many, dreadful and terrifying. So go slowly, charioteer, and guard the rear.\""}},{"n":35,"text":"मयि स्थिते च समरे निरुद्धेषु च पाण्डुषु ।\nपुनरावर्तते तूर्णं मामकं बलमोजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"While I hold my ground in the battle and the Pandavas are checked, my army will rally quickly and with vigor.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"तच्छ्रुत्वा तव पुत्रस्य शूराग्र्यसदृशं वचः ।\nसारथिर्हेमसंछन्नाञ्शनैरश्वानचोदयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing those words of your son, worthy of the foremost hero, the charioteer slowly urged on the horses draped in gold."}},{"n":37,"text":"गजाश्वरथिभिर्हीनास्त्यक्तात्मानः पदातयः ।\nएकविंशतिसाहस्राः संयुगायावतस्थिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Twenty-one thousand foot-soldiers, without elephants, horses or chariots, careless of their lives, stood ready for battle."}},{"n":38,"text":"नानादेशसमुद्भूता नानारञ्जितवाससः ।\nअवस्थितास्तदा योधाः प्रार्थयन्तो महद्यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those warriors, born in many lands and dressed in many colors, stood firm, seeking great glory."}},{"n":39,"text":"तेषामापततां तत्र संहृष्टानां परस्परम् ।\nसंमर्दः सुमहाञ्जज्ञे घोररूपो भयानकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they charged at one another with joy, a vast, terrible and fearsome clash arose."}},{"n":40,"text":"भीमसेनं तदा राजन्धृष्टद्युम्नं च पार्षतम् ।\nबलेन चतुरङ्गेण नानादेश्या न्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, men of many lands with a four-division force held back Bhimasena and Dhrishtadyumna, son of Prishata."}},{"n":41,"text":"भीममेवाभ्यवर्तन्त रणेऽन्ये तु पदातयः ।\nप्रक्ष्वेड्यास्फोट्य संहृष्टा वीरलोकं यियासवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Other foot-soldiers turned on Bhima alone, roaring and slapping their arms in glee, eager to reach the world of heroes."}},{"n":42,"text":"आसाद्य भीमसेनं तु संरब्धा युद्धदुर्मदाः ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रा विनेदुर्हि नान्यां चाकथयन्कथाम् ।\nपरिवार्य रणे भीमं निजघ्नुस्ते समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching Bhimasena, the Dhartarashtras, furious and mad for battle, shouted, speaking of nothing else; surrounding Bhima in the fight, they struck at him from every side."}},{"n":43,"text":"स वध्यमानः समरे पदातिगणसंवृतः ।\nन चचाल रथोपस्थे मैनाक इव पर्वतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though struck in the battle and ringed by those foot-soldiers, he did not stir on his chariot platform, like the mountain Mainaka."}},{"n":44,"text":"ते तु क्रुद्धा महाराज पाण्डवस्य महारथम् ।\nनिग्रहीतुं प्रचक्रुर्हि योधांश्चान्यानवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Enraged, O great king, they tried to seize the great chariot of the Pandava and kept the other warriors away."}},{"n":45,"text":"अक्रुध्यत रणे भीमस्तैस्तदा पर्यवस्थितैः ।\nसोऽवतीर्य रथात्तूर्णं पदातिः समवस्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima grew angry in the fight at those who stood around him; he leapt quickly from his chariot and stood on foot."}},{"n":46,"text":"जातरूपपरिच्छन्नां प्रगृह्य महतीं गदाम् ।\nअवधीत्तावकान्योधान्दण्डपाणिरिवान्तकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up a great mace covered in gold, he killed your warriors like Death himself with his staff in hand."}},{"n":47,"text":"रथाश्वद्विपहीनांस्तु तान्भीमो गदया बली ।\nएकविंशतिसाहस्रान्पदातीनवपोथयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With his mace the mighty Bhima crushed those twenty-one thousand foot-soldiers, who had no chariots, horses or elephants."}},{"n":48,"text":"हत्वा तत्पुरुषानीकं भीमः सत्यपराक्रमः ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नं पुरस्कृत्य नचिरात्प्रत्यदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having destroyed that force of men, Bhima, true in valor, was soon seen again with Dhrishtadyumna placed in front."}},{"n":49,"text":"पादाता निहता भूमौ शिश्यिरे रुधिरोक्षिताः ।\nसंभग्ना इव वातेन कर्णिकाराः सुपुष्पिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The slain foot-soldiers lay on the ground drenched in blood, like blossoming karnikara trees broken by the wind."}},{"n":50,"text":"नानापुष्पस्रजोपेता नानाकुण्डलधारिणः ।\nनानाजात्या हतास्तत्र नानादेशसमागताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wearing garlands of many flowers and many kinds of earrings, men of many races, gathered from many lands, lay slain there."}},{"n":51,"text":"पताकाध्वजसंछन्नं पदातीनां महद्बलम् ।\nनिकृत्तं विबभौ तत्र घोररूपं भयानकम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great force of foot-soldiers, covered with pennants and banners, shone terrible and fearsome, cut to pieces."}},{"n":52,"text":"युधिष्ठिरपुरोगास्तु सर्वसैन्यमहारथाः ।\nअभ्यधावन्महात्मानं पुत्रं दुर्योधनं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the great chariot-fighters of the army, with Yudhishthira at their head, ran toward your son, the great-souled Duryodhana."}},{"n":53,"text":"ते सर्वे तावकान्दृष्ट्वा महेष्वासान्पराङ्मुखान् ।\nनाभ्यवर्तन्त ते पुत्रं वेलेव मकरालयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing your great archers turning away, they all failed to confront your son, as the shore does not cross the ocean, home of sea-monsters."}},{"n":54,"text":"तदद्भुतमपश्याम तव पुत्रस्य पौरुषम् ।\nयदेकं सहिताः पार्था न शेकुरतिवर्तितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw that marvelous manliness of your son: the Parthas, though united, could not get past him alone."}},{"n":55,"text":"नातिदूरापयातं तु कृतबुद्धिं पलायने ।\nदुर्योधनः स्वकं सैन्यमब्रवीद्भृशविक्षतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Not far off, Duryodhana saw his badly wounded army resolved on flight, and spoke to them."}},{"n":56,"text":"न तं देशं प्रपश्यामि पृथिव्यां पर्वतेषु वा ।\nयत्र यातान्न वो हन्युः पाण्डवाः किं सृतेन वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I see no place on earth, even among the mountains, where, if you fled, the Pandavas would not kill you. What is the use of running?\""}},{"n":57,"text":"अल्पं च बलमेतेषां कृष्णौ च भृशविक्षतौ ।\nयदि सर्वेऽत्र तिष्ठामो ध्रुवो नो विजयो भवेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Their force is small, and the two Krishnas are badly wounded. If we all stand here, victory will surely be ours.\""}},{"n":58,"text":"विप्रयातांस्तु वो भिन्नान्पाण्डवाः कृतकिल्बिषान् ।\nअनुसृत्य हनिष्यन्ति श्रेयो नः समरे स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"If you scatter and flee, you who have done them wrong, the Pandavas will chase and kill you. Better for us to stand and fight.\""}},{"n":59,"text":"शृणुध्वं क्षत्रियाः सर्वे यावन्तः स्थ समागताः ।\nयदा शूरं च भीरुं च मारयत्यन्तकः सदा ।\nको नु मूढो न युध्येत पुरुषः क्षत्रियब्रुवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Listen, all you kshatriyas who are gathered here. Since Death always kills both the brave and the coward, what foolish man who calls himself a kshatriya would not fight?\""}},{"n":60,"text":"श्रेयो नो भीमसेनस्य क्रुद्धस्य प्रमुखे स्थितम् ।\nसुखः सांग्रामिको मृत्युः क्षत्रधर्मेण युध्यताम् ।\nजित्वेह सुखमाप्नोति हतः प्रेत्य महत्फलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"It is better for us to stand before the angry Bhimasena. A death in battle is easy for those who fight by the warrior's law. A man who wins gains happiness here; if killed, he gains a great reward beyond.\""}},{"n":61,"text":"न युद्धधर्माच्छ्रेयान्वै पन्थाः स्वर्गस्य कौरवाः ।\nअचिरेण जिताँल्लोकान्हतो युद्धे समश्नुते ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O Kauravas, no road to heaven is better than the duty of battle. One killed in war quickly enjoys the worlds he has won.\""}},{"n":62,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु वचनं तस्य पूजयित्वा च पार्थिवाः ।\nपुनरेवान्ववर्तन्त पाण्डवानाततायिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing his words, the kings honored him and turned back again to face the Pandavas, their murderous foes."}},{"n":63,"text":"तानापतत एवाशु व्यूढानीकाः प्रहारिणः ।\nप्रत्युद्ययुस्तदा पार्था जयगृध्राः प्रहारिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they charged, the Pandavas, hard-hitting and eager for victory, advanced to meet them swiftly with their ranks arrayed."}},{"n":64,"text":"धनंजयो रथेनाजावभ्यवर्तत वीर्यवान् ।\nविश्रुतं त्रिषु लोकेषु गाण्डीवं विक्षिपन्धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Dhananjaya attacked in his chariot, shaking his bow Gandiva, famed in the three worlds."}},{"n":65,"text":"माद्रीपुत्रौ च शकुनिं सात्यकिश्च महाबलः ।\nजवेनाभ्यपतन्हृष्टा यतो वै तावकं बलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two sons of Madri, with the mighty Satyaki, rushed joyfully against Shakuni, to where your force stood."}}]}]}